WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
You've saved all summer
for your first car.

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.460
Online, you find two listings:

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.620
same model, same year, same price.

4
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.230
Both sellers say theirs runs great.

5
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.790
What would you offer?

6
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.960
Now flip it.

7
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.780
You're the seller, and your
car really is in great shape.

8
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.450
The offers you get are
less than it's worth.

9
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.120
So why can a used car that runs perfectly

10
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.800
be hard to sell for what it is worth?

11
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.810
In this mission, you'll work
out exactly what a careful

12
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.650
buyer is willing to pay.

13
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.580
Then you'll use a graph lab:

14
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.570
slide the share of good cars
and watch the market respond.

15
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.850
Your mission: explain why
a great car can struggle

16
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.250
to get a fair price.
